-- title:
--   Gauss prime lies in every supersingular maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $(q:\overline{\mathbb Q})\in A.\mathrm{nonunits}$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and write $A_0:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`; let $\pi_0\in k_0$ lie in $A$ and assume: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, $A_0$ is henselian, its residue field is algebraically closed, and every element of $A$ differs from some element of $k_0\cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime, $\ell'\ne q$, $\ell'\ge 3$, $\ell'\nmid M'$, let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity admitting an embedding $k_0\hookrightarrow\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((q))$ equal to `laurentBaseChange` of the level-$(q\ell')^2M'$ function field `xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M')`, with $H$ the kernel of the reduction of unit groups `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul (q*ℓ') M')`, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $A_0\to k_0\to K$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion `coeffEmb ↥k₀ ModularCurve.jq`. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ admitting a presentation $f\cdot y=x$ with $x,y\in A_0[[q]]$ (pushed into $k_0((q))$) and $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A_0$, the Gauss ring. Let $y'$ be a maximal ideal of the chart algebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥A₀ ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) containing the image of $\pi_0$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ (with decidable equality) and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from that chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y'$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then every $h$ in the chart algebra whose image in $K$ lies in $W_0.\mathrm{nonunits}$ belongs to $y'$.
--
--   The prime $C'\cap\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ cut out on the chart algebra by the Gauss valuation is the generic point of the component of the special fibre passing through the cusp at infinity; the assertion is that this prime specialises to every supersingular closed point of the special fibre carrying $\pi_0$. It is used in the construction of places and ring homomorphisms on the chart algebra at supersingular points for the level-$q\ell'$ integral model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin.lean

